{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-223387",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $523,$ we have that \n\n$$\n52-2(3)=52-6=46\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $523$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $532,$ we have that \n\n$$\n53-2(2)=53-4=49\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $532$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $501,$ we have that \n\n$$\n50-2(1)=50-2=48\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $501$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
